{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9ilz2gn15","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"sumAmounts rows: amount string feed has two locale formats — Number()/parseFloat misparses comma-decimal rows returning wrong total","summary":"sumAmounts(rows) parses each amount string from the billing feed. The amount rows use two formats: (1) en-US: dot as decimal separator — parse with parseFloat directly. (2) de-DE: comma as decimal separator, dot as thousands — parseFloat(\"99,90\") returns 99 not 99.9, parseFloat(\"1.234,56\") returns 1.234 not 1234.56. The sumAmounts total is WRONG if rows with comma-decimal amounts are parsed naively. NaN rows from parseFloat return 0 and are silently skipped — no exception thrown, the total Number is just wrong. Fix: per amount row, if string includes comma, normalize (remove dot-thousands, swap comma→dot) before parseFloat. Return total rounded to 2 decimal places. Example: sumAmounts([{amount:\"99,90\"}]) must return 99.9 not 0.","created_by":"self-learning-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T13:10:04.744Z","vec":[-0.010858066380023956,0.026572752743959427,0.04169496148824692,-0.04793861135840416,-0.05577104911208153,-0.08048463612794876,-0.020041758194565773,0.016352713108062744,0.06908094137907028,0.003925742115825415,0.0033138261642307043,-0.13553903996944427,-0.0520501509308815,0.03815614804625511,0.004859263077378273,-0.07137103378772736,-0.04476870968937874,0.005349649116396904,0.04484957456588745,0.012400870211422443,0.061623528599739075,0.04941701516509056,0.002782421186566353,0.005901625845581293,0.07053358852863312,0.06246808543801308,-0.014694435521960258,0.03400077298283577,-0.016060633584856987,-0.010905997827649117,-0.06056826561689377,0.036464106291532516,0.05543893575668335,0.002306167269125581,-0.01145361177623272,-0.04113176837563515,0.0031769012566655874,0.011306428350508213,0.014110054820775986,0.03336646035313606,0.054234229028224945,-0.035008691251277924,0.07639949768781662,-0.056418467313051224,0.04064705967